  "notes": "Compac ATV R2 (manufacturer SCBC, device R2, Realtek), Android TV 9 (API 28),\nfirmware PTT1.201001.001, 2 GB RAM. Same SCBC platform as examples/sanyo-atv-r2.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/compac-atv-r2/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/compac-atv-r2/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher is com.google.android.tvlauncher. It is not in this list: disable it only once a\nreplacement Home is installed (launcher/build-and-install.sh does that in the right order).\n\nNotes from this TV:\n- Kept in use: Google Assistant (katniss), FastCast Miracast (com.creative.fastscreen.tv),\nfirmware updates (com.apps.ota, com.apps.authota), Spotify, YouTube Music, Play Movies, Play Games.\n- Not touched, unclear: com.apps.esticker (ShowService overlay, likely store-demo stickers) and\nio.mimi.tvapp (Mimi hearing-profile sound app, bundles Mixpanel).\n- Leave alone, as on the SANYO: com.realtek.tv.* (inputs, tuner), com.apps.smartkey / virtualkey /\nbluetoothremote / com.functions.autopair (remote), com.apps.puresound, com.apps.usbmediaplayer.\n- The saved Wi-Fi network belongs to android.uid.system, not setupwraith.\nSCBC / Google telemetry and feedback",
